Z||000000||Formula88||02-08-2001||10:50 PM||||Ok, I searched, but didn't find anything.  Anyone here have the Fi-Euro gated shifter in thier Fiero?  How do you like it?  I'm thinking about getting one for my car, but I want to hear what other people have to say about it, first.  Also, does it look as good in person as the pics look?  Is it anything more than a chrome shift lever and a gated plate?  I could probably make one myself, but if FOCOA's Fi-Euro is a quality piece, then that'll save me the work.  Any feedback?  Please post pics of it if you have one!<P>------------------<BR>We all come into this world the same way; naked, screaming, and covered in blood.  If you're lucky, it doesn't have to end there.||||reg||5
Z||000001||TwisT||02-08-2001||10:57 PM||||OK...  no personal experience here,  but I have dug into this in the past.  The "Euro-shifter" for the Fiero LOOKS awesome...  but that's about it.  A true "gate" shifter is exactly that;  it operates by using a succession of levers to the transmission to change gears (think Ferrari).  Our beloved Fieros use cables.  So,  in a nut-shell,  your "gate" shifter looks great but functions just as it is...  a standard "cable" style shifter.  You won't have the gate effect at all when shifting,  i.e.,  your shift-rod won't follow the gate pattern but vaguely.  Sitting still in a car show might be impressive tho.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Formula88||02-08-2001||11:01 PM||||Yea, I knew I'd be limited by the cable shifter setup.  I was just curious is it was well done and looked good in the car.  Also, does it improve shift quality at all?  Any shorter throw on shifts, etc?  Definately not going to feel like a good Hurst linkage on a M22 Rockcrusher!  Oh, now that feels good!<P>------------------<BR>We all come into this world the same way; naked, screaming, and covered in blood.  If you're lucky, it doesn't have to end there.||||reg||1
Z||000003||turbo86se||02-09-2001||01:16 AM||||I had one in my old '85 coupe. I absolutely LOVED it!! It looked great and made me feel like I was driving a Ferrari. If either of my Fieros was a stick, I'd buy one again in a heartbeat. I got mine from IRM.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=226077&a=1676320&p=20236791"> ||||reg||1
